@* A BitLink written with raw HTML attributes beside its own parameters. BitLink collects what it was not
   given a parameter for into HtmlAttributes itself rather than through CaptureUnmatchedValues, so splatting
   is what a test has to go through to observe what the component does with an attribute it did not write.
   The splat comes last because Blazor deduplicates the two case-insensitively: an unset Target written after
   it would take a splatted target straight back off again, before BitLink ever saw it. *@
<BitLink Href="@Href" Target="@Target" @attributes="Attributes">bit</BitLink>

@code {
    [Parameter] public Dictionary<string, object> Attributes { get; set; } = [];

    [Parameter] public string? Href { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public string? Target { get; set; }
}
